From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: add the multi-duelist interface for phase 2

This patch adds the interface that the later phase 2 core patches use.
With 2 duelists every message byte, Lua result and random call stays
the same.

field.h:
- opponent_of(p) gets default arguments __builtin_FILE() and
  __builtin_LINE(). Under YGO_N_TRAP it prints the caller's file and
  line and aborts when n_duelists > 2. Without the define the body is
  the stock 1 - p. All callers still pass one argument.
- next_in_turn_order(p) returns the next duelist clockwise that is
  alive, starting at p + 1 (mod n_duelists), or p when no other duelist
  is alive. With no eliminated duelist the first candidate is
  (p + 1) % n_duelists, the old result, for every p.
- lp_ref(p) returns the LP of p's team (player[team_of(p)].lp). It is
  an accessor only. No LP site uses it yet.
- field::first_attack_turn (default 2) and before_first_attack_turn():
  turn_id >= 1 && turn_id < first_attack_turn. With the default this is
  the stock test turn_id == 1 for every int16_t value.
- processor::battle_defender and processor::response_anchor, both
  DUELIST_NONE. Nothing reads them yet.
- field::eliminate(p) declared. The body only sets
  player[p].eliminated for a duelist in play.

First-attack sites (2): field.cpp is_able_to_enter_bp (turn_id != 1
becomes !before_first_attack_turn()) and processor.cpp IdleCommand
(turn_id == 1 becomes before_first_attack_turn()). The short-circuit
order is the same. Not changed: the first-turn draw skip in the Turn
processor (turn_id > 1) and the tag_swap check (turn_id != 1). They are
not attack checks.

Constructor: every player entry, also player[2] and player[3], gets
team = index and eliminated = false. The unused entries come from
OCG_Player{} (LP 0, counts 0). The per-duelist arrays in core and infos
are value-initialised, so entries 2 and 3 are zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 field.cpp     | 15 +++++++++++++--
 field.h       | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 processor.cpp |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/field.cpp b/field.cpp
index d479725..d3b0110 100644
--- a/field.cpp
+++ b/field.cpp
@@ -101,8 +101,14 @@ field::field(duel* _pduel, const OCG_DuelOptions& options) :pduel(_pduel), playe
 	core.duel_options = options.flags;
 	// Every entry, also the unused ones, so that a later n_duelists value needs no other set up.
 	// This loop has no side effect (no message, no Lua call, no random number).
-	for(uint8_t p = 0; p < MAX_DUELISTS; ++p)
+	// The unused entries player[2] and player[3] are built from OCG_Player{} (LP 0, counts 0, empty
+	// zones, not eliminated). Debug.SetupDuelists gives them the starting values of player 0.
+	// Every per-duelist array in core is zero because core is value-initialised (processor core{}),
+	// and the arrays in infos use {}.
+	for(uint8_t p = 0; p < MAX_DUELISTS; ++p) {
 		player[p].team = p;
+		player[p].eliminated = false;
+	}
 	nil_event.event_code = 0;
 	nil_event.event_cards = nullptr;
 	nil_event.event_player = PLAYER_NONE;
@@ -111,6 +117,11 @@ field::field(duel* _pduel, const OCG_DuelOptions& options) :pduel(_pduel), playe
 	nil_event.reason_effect = nullptr;
 	nil_event.reason_player = PLAYER_NONE;
 }
+void field::eliminate(uint8_t p) {
+	if(!is_duelist(p))
+		return;
+	player[p].eliminated = true;
+}
 void field::reload_field_info() {
 	auto message = pduel->new_message(MSG_RELOAD_FIELD);
 	message->write<uint32_t>(core.duel_options);
@@ -3311,7 +3322,7 @@ int32_t field::check_spself_from_hand_trigger(const chain& ch) const {
 	return TRUE;
 }
 int32_t field::is_able_to_enter_bp() {
-	return (is_flag(DUEL_ATTACK_FIRST_TURN) || infos.turn_id != 1 || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_BP_FIRST_TURN))
+	return (is_flag(DUEL_ATTACK_FIRST_TURN) || !before_first_attack_turn() || is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_BP_FIRST_TURN))
 	        && infos.phase < PHASE_BATTLE_START
 	        && !is_player_affected_by_effect(infos.turn_player, EFFECT_CANNOT_BP);
 }
